The blue curve shows a retained branch of $y=\tan x$. State its domain using bracket notation, and explain why this branch has an inverse function.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=7mm,>=stealth]
\definecolor{branchBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[->,draw=black] (0,-3.3)--(0,3.5) node[above,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$y$};
\draw[->,draw=black] (-0.3,0)--(6.7,0) node[right,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$x$};
\draw[dashed,draw=black] (1.570796,-3.1)--(1.570796,3.1);
\draw[dashed,draw=black] (4.712389,-3.1)--(4.712389,3.1);
\foreach \a/\lab in {1.570796/{\frac{\pi}{2}},3.141593/{\pi},4.712389/{\frac{3\pi}{2}},6.283185/{2\pi}} {
\draw[draw=black] (\a,-0.08)--(\a,0.08);
\path (\a,-0.12) node[below,fill=white,inner sep=2pt,text=black,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\lab$};
}
\foreach \b in {-1,1} {
\draw[draw=black] (-0.08,\b)--(0.08,\b);
\path (-0.1,\b) node[left,text=black,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\b$};
}
\draw[<->,very thick,draw=branchBlue] plot[domain=1.892547:4.390638,samples=100] (\x,{tan(\x*180/pi)});
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
